be there in an outfit that coordinates * my* way—because my presence matters more than the fabric I’m wearing.\"* ### ❤️ **The real takeaway:** **Your comfort and autonomy matter**. A loving family shouldn’t make you feel like you * have* to sacrifice your own needs for \"coordination.\" True togetherness comes from * choice*, not obligation. If they truly care about you, they’ll respect your boundaries. And if they don’t? That’s their issue—not yours. > * \"Family is about love, not uniformity. You don’t have to wear the same fabric to be part of the same heart.\"* > — *Adapted from a wise friend who navigated this exact situation* Would you like help crafting a specific message to share with your family? I’m happy to brainstorm phrasing that’s kind but clear. You’ve got this. 💛"
